-- title:
--   Stalk fibre ring of a finite morphism is zero-dimensional
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ and $Y$ be schemes (in a fixed universe), let $g : X \to Y$ be a morphism which is finite, assume $Y$ is locally Noetherian, and let $x$ be a point of $X$. Consider the induced map on stalks $g^{\sharp}_x : \mathcal{O}_{Y, g(x)} \to \mathcal{O}_{X,x}$, where $g(x)$ denotes the image of $x$ under the map of underlying topological spaces, and let $\mathfrak{m}_{g(x)} \subseteq \mathcal{O}_{Y,g(x)}$ be the maximal ideal of that local ring. The assertion is that the Krull dimension of the quotient of $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak{m}_{g(x)}$ under $g^{\sharp}_x$, i.e.
--   $$\operatorname{ringKrullDim}\bigl(\mathcal{O}_{X,x} / \mathfrak{m}_{g(x)}\mathcal{O}_{X,x}\bigr),$$
--   is equal to $0$; here the dimension is taken in $\mathbb{N}\cup\{\pm\infty\}$, so the statement includes in particular that the quotient ring is nonzero (the empty spectrum would have dimension $-\infty$).
--
--   This is the local form of the statement that a finite morphism has zero-dimensional (indeed Artinian) fibres: the fibre ring of $g$ at $x$ over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_{Y,g(x)}$ is zero-dimensional and nonzero. It is used in the treatment of abelian schemes and relative group laws, where flatness of certain finite morphisms is deduced from dimension and depth information at stalks.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_IsFinite_ringKrullDim_stalk_quotient_eq_zero.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry IsLocalRing

theorem AlgebraicGeometry.IsFinite.ringKrullDim_stalk_quotient_eq_zero
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : X ⟶ Y) [IsFinite g] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] (x : X) :
    ringKrullDim ((X.presheaf.stalk x) ⧸
      (maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (g.base x))).map (g.stalkMap x).hom) = 0 := by sorry
